/ MARIE bitmap framebuffer demonstration.
/ Post-course reimplementation: this file is not based on the original assessment template.
/
/ Display model assumed by MARIE simulator:
/   16 x 16 words at 0F00..0FFF
/ Each glyph is 4 x 8 = 32 words, row-major.
/
/ The core idea is deliberately small: clear the framebuffer, then copy a 4x8 glyph
/ into display memory via indirect addressing. The Python reference model demonstrates
/ complete multi-character layout and wrapping.

        JnS ClearDisplay

/ Paint a sample H at the top-left corner.
        Load GlyphHAddr
        Store GlyphPtr
        Load DisplayBase
        Store DisplayPtr
        JnS PaintGlyph

        Halt

/ ------------------------------------------------------------------
/ ClearDisplay: fill 0F00..0FFF with FFFF (background)
ClearDisplay, HEX 0000
        Load DisplayBase
        Store ClearPtr
ClearLoop, Load Background
        StoreI ClearPtr
        Load ClearPtr
        Add One
        Store ClearPtr
        Load ClearPtr
        Subt DisplayEndPlusOne
        Skipcond 400
        Jump ClearLoop
        JumpI ClearDisplay

/ ------------------------------------------------------------------
/ PaintGlyph: copy a 4x8 row-major glyph to the framebuffer.
/ Inputs: GlyphPtr and DisplayPtr.
/ After each 4-pixel row, advance 12 extra words because display width is 16.
PaintGlyph, HEX 0000
        Clear
        Store PixelCount
        Clear
        Store ColumnCount
PaintLoop, LoadI GlyphPtr
        StoreI DisplayPtr

        Load GlyphPtr
        Add One
        Store GlyphPtr

        Load DisplayPtr
        Add One
        Store DisplayPtr

        Load ColumnCount
        Add One
        Store ColumnCount
        Subt Four
        Skipcond 400
        Jump SkipRowAdvance

        Clear
        Store ColumnCount
        Load DisplayPtr
        Add Twelve
        Store DisplayPtr

SkipRowAdvance, Load PixelCount
        Add One
        Store PixelCount
        Subt ThirtyTwo
        Skipcond 400
        Jump PaintLoop
        JumpI PaintGlyph

/ ------------------------------------------------------------------
DisplayBase, HEX 0F00
DisplayEndPlusOne, HEX 1000
Background, HEX FFFF
One, DEC 1
Four, DEC 4
Twelve, DEC 12
ThirtyTwo, DEC 32
ClearPtr, HEX 0000
GlyphPtr, HEX 0000
DisplayPtr, HEX 0000
PixelCount, DEC 0
ColumnCount, DEC 0

/ A single self-contained H glyph for the assembly demo.
/ Foreground uses F00F; background uses 0000.
GlyphH, HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX F00F
        HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX F00F
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
        HEX 0000
GlyphHAddr, ADR GlyphH
